HST Office: real Excel files keep their VBA project; new Writer VBA proposes .odt.

Every save of an .xlsm or .xls regenerated the project, in upstream and in every HST release, dropping
the compiled cache, and a real form was lost or, with the form export, no longer loads in Excel. Now:
- .xlsm import stores the project as it is in the file, as .xls import does already.
- A project with unchanged macros is written back: an .xlsm to an .xlsm byte for byte.
- A project with UserForms is written back also when macros were edited, because real Excel does not
  load forms HST writes; Save As asks first, as it does for Word files. Edited macros without forms are
  written as before: real Excel runs plain macros HST writes (owner's test).
- Save As: real Word shows no macros in a project HST writes (owner's test), so new VBA in Writer
  proposes .odt, and choosing .docm or .doc warns. A project read from a Word file stays.

License: these upstream files remain under their original license (MPL-2.0).
Test: tests/runtime/check-vba-keep-word-project.py, tests/runtime/check-vba-save-format.py.
